RGB20SX: the device tree names the unit "Powkiddy RGB20SX" (it said "Powkiddy RGB30").
Moss keys its device quirks on this string (QUIRK_DEVICE), so the quirks folder is copied under the new name too.

--- linux.orig/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-rgb30-linux.dts
+++ linux/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-rgb30-linux.dts
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
 #include "rk3568-linux.dtsi"
 
 / {
-	model = "Powkiddy RGB30";
+	model = "Powkiddy RGB20SX";
 	compatible = "rockchip,rk3566-evb2-lp4x-v11", "rockchip,rk3566";
 
 	adc_keys: adc-keys {
